# CONTRIBUTING Contribute-Guide SoT

[`CONTRIBUTING.md`](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) is the **human contribute-guide SoT**: prerequisites, local setup, quality gate + recommended DX, contribute workflow (small vs feature), commits/PRs, Issues/SECURITY pointers, and a documentation map of links.

It is **not** a Design SoT, directory layout map, coverage SoT, exit-code SoT, adapter catalog, or fragile-risk catalog.

## Ownership matrix

| Change type | Destination |
| ----------- | ----------- |
| Setup, gate, DX scripts, PR/contribute workflow | **CONTRIBUTING.md** |
| Exit codes, agent policies, skills/agents inventory | **AGENTS.md** |
| Directory layout / public API | **STRUCTURE.md** |
| Coverage thresholds / fixtures / mock boundaries | **TESTING.md** |
| Adapter / spawn ownership | **INTEGRATIONS.md** |
| Fragile risks / RT / mitigations | **CONCERNS.md** |
| Modules, pipelines, contracts | **ARCHITECTURE.md** |
| Milestone status, feature history | **ROADMAP.md** / `.specs/features/` |
| Decisions, deferred ideas, blockers | **STATE.md** |

## Forbidden in CONTRIBUTING.md

- Milestone tags: `\bM\d+\b` (e.g. `M71`)
- Directory trees (box-drawing `├──` / `└──`) — link STRUCTURE instead
- Coverage threshold tables / `Coverage thresholds` sections — link TESTING instead
- Local exit-code tables or `!= 0` shorthand — link AGENTS § Validation (CLI)
- `## Architecture boundaries` / adapter location tables — link INTEGRATIONS
- `## Fragile areas` risk tables — link CONCERNS
- Design SoT dumps, flag encyclopedias, changelog voice

## Allowed

- `HOTSPOT-*` as a **naming convention** when describing feature specs
- Gate `pnpm build && pnpm test`, recommended `typecheck` / `lint` / `format:check`
- Mermaid contribute flowchart; focused branch + PR what/why/test plan
- Short convention bullets + links; Documentation map of links only
- One “no CI in v1” stance sentence

## Sync rule

When living docs change after Execute:

1. Update CONTRIBUTING **only** when gate, DX scripts, prerequisites, or contribute/PR workflow changed — otherwise skip.
2. **Do not** mirror STRUCTURE, TESTING, INTEGRATIONS, CONCERNS, or the AGENTS exit-code table — link those SoTs.
3. Self-check: *Would this table/tree go stale when code layout or thresholds change?* If yes → wrong file (link the SoT).

Editorial lint: [living-sot-doc.mjs](../hooks/lib/living-sot-doc.mjs) `lintContributingDoc` (hooks + `pnpm hooks:smoke`).
